00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:26.820
That same cycle aware thinking appears in our next segment on sector rotation.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:34.900
Imagine you added a broad TSX ETF last month when tariff headlines first surfaced and your order filled at the open.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:43.560
The actual path from click to fill involved the ETFs underlying banking and mining holdings repricing faster than the index average

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:46.740
because those sectors lead early cycle rotations.

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:52.340
Sector rotation works by matching economic phases to historical outperformers.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:56.200
Financials and industrials tend to lead in early expansion.

00:04:56.940 --> 00:05:00.260
Defensive such as utilities and staples hold up near peak.

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:04.160
Energy and materials often bottom first in contraction.

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:12.300
Use the yield curve slope, PMI readings above 50 and same day volume above the 20 day average before sizing.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:19.000
In a post-COVID economy, the pattern can compress because fiscal stimulus overrides traditional cycle timing.

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:23.980
Recheck the yield curve and PMI signals every quarter before rebalancing.

